<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Except in the generic warm start result <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>
and its consequence <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>, throughout the remainder of the paper
<math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) holds pointwise.
For most of the paper, we normalize <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>; this can be achieved by rescaling.</p>
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity of exposition, we initially allow ourselves access to proximal queries to <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, in addition to queries to <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math>.
For step size <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, one proximal query returns</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\coloneqq\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\Bigl\{V(x)+\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">argmin</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\coloneqq\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\Bigl\{V(x)+\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The sampling analogue of the proximal operator is the restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO), which is the distribution</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{a,y}(\mathrm{d}x)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{a,y}(\mathrm{d}x)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
We also use</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(P\mathbin{\|}Q)\coloneqq\int\log\bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}P\,,\qquad W_{2}^{2}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{(X,Y)}\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>dP</mi><mi>dQ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dP</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\mathbin{\|}Q)\coloneqq\int\log\bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}P\,,\qquad W_{2}^{2}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{(X,Y)}\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with the usual value <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for KL without absolute continuity; the
infimum in the definition of <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is over all couplings of <math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proximal optimality gives
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{y}(u)\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\sqrt{\eta}\,\langle\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{y}(u)\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\sqrt{\eta}\,\langle\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq\nabla^{2}\rho_{y}\preceq\eta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq\nabla^{2}\rho_{y}\preceq\eta I</annotation></semantics></math>, and under <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X-x_{y}^{+})/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X-x_{y}^{+})/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> has density
proportional to <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\mapsto e^{-\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2-\rho_{y}(u)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto e^{-\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2-\rho_{y}(u)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Call this law <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\mathsf{r}_{y},\mathsf{N}(0,I))\leqslant\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\lVert\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\rVert^{2}]}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\lVert U\rVert^{2}}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\mathsf{r}_{y},\mathsf{N}(0,I))\leqslant\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\lVert\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\rVert^{2}]}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\lVert U\rVert^{2}}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, the first inequality combines Talagrand’s inequality for the standard
Gaussian with the Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality; the second uses that
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\rho_{y}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\rho_{y}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\rho_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\rho_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz; and the last
follows by integration by parts since <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly
log-concave with its mode at <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
